      "side": 1,
      "message": "Confirmed, and thanks for the precise pointer - traced it end to end and reproduced it here.\n\nTerminate only rewinds rows current at that moment (`get_current_schedule`), and the admin batch/PATCH paths can leave future-dated rows on a self-schedule assignment. The counter has no cloud scope either, so a dead assignment keeps paying for itself out of the model pool for the whole fleet: a free same-model host is rejected with \"Model X has reached its self-scheduling limit\" and is capped out of the can_self_schedule\u003dtrue listing. A/B verified: adding the filter flips that 400 back to 201, and the same stale row on a still-active assignment correctly keeps the 400.\n\nNext patchset adds `Assignment.active.is_(True)` to `count_ss_schedules_by_model_overlap`, same form as ab3dc63 did for `get_current_schedule` (#746), with a regression test that fails on PS7 as it stands, and I will rebase onto development so #746 sits in the stack.\n\nThis does not touch precedence: admin bookings supersede self-scheduling and are never gated by the pool, which only applies to self-service assignments (including admin batch windows on them, per the docs). Once the self-service assignment is terminated, the pool needs to follow the supersede instead of charging the model for rows nobody owns.\n\nThe leftover-rows-still-lock-out-their-own-hosts part (`is_host_available` has no active filter) is pre-existing, out of scope for this one, and I will track it with the #746 follow-ups.",
